// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Network Optix Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Network Optix Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 10137 or greater.</li>\n<li>Network Optix Witness VMS version 4.2.0.32840 or greater.</li>\n<li>Network Optix Witness VMS version 5.0.0.35745 or greater.</li>\n<li>Network Optix Witness VMS version 5.1.0.37466 or greater.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 320\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"245\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"245\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"245\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <rect x=\"330\" y=\"80\" width=\"150\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f2f3f6\" stroke=\"#9aa0ac\"/>\n  <text x=\"405\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">Nx Witness VMS</text>\n  <rect x=\"360\" y=\"220\" width=\"130\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#0b0f19\"/>\n  <text x=\"425\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"480\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"600\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrN)\"/>\n  <text x=\"500\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">Object Metadata Display<tspan x=\"500\" dy=\"13\">Event Notification</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"22\">&#128241;</text>\n  <text x=\"620\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">Client, Mobile App</text>\n  <line x1=\"405\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <text x=\"440\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#7a4f10\">AI Metadata &amp; Event<tspan x=\"440\" dy=\"13\">with AIBridge NX Plugin</tspan></text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrN\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>IP cameras stream RTSP video to both Nx VMS and AIBridge; AIBridge analyzes it via AI apps and sends metadata &amp; events to Nx VMS using the AIBridge NX plugin</figcaption>\n</div>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>IP cameras send their video stream to both the Nx VMS and AIBridge.</li>\n<li>AIBridge analyzes the received video stream using its AI apps.</li>\n<li>AIBridge sends metadata and events to Nx VMS using the AIBridge NX plugin.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>2. AIBridge NX VMS Plugin Installation and Configuration</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.1 Installing NX Witness VMS</h3>\n<p>Install NX Witness VMS v5.X or greater. Both a server and a client are required, since the client is used during configuration.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 Installing the AIBridge Plugin (on Windows)</h3>\n<p><strong>Stop the NX Witness server.</strong> Right-click the tray icon and select <strong>Stop Server</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:260px;\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\">\n  <div class=\"modal-body\" style=\"font-size:12px;\">\n    <div>Server Web Page</div>\n    <div style=\"margin-top:6px;\">Stop Server (started)</div>\n    <div style=\"margin-top:6px;\">Show Server Log</div>\n    <hr style=\"border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:8px 0;\">\n    <div>Quit</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>NX Witness tray icon menu</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>Download the AIBridge analytics plugin from the customer portal and unzip it.</p>\n<p>Copy the <code>aibridge_analytics_plugin.dll</code> file to <code>{NxInstallPath}\\plugins\\</code>. This is typically located at <code>C:\\Program Files\\Network Optix\\Nx Witness\\MediaServer\\plugins</code>.</p>\n<p>Copy the <code>libzmq-mt-4_3_3.dll</code> file to <code>{NxInstallPath}\\</code>. This is typically located at <code>C:\\Program Files\\Network Optix\\Nx Witness\\MediaServer\\</code>.</p>\n<p>Download and install <a href=\"https://aka.ms/vs/16/release/vc_redist.x64.exe\">vc_redist.x64.exe</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Start the NX Witness server.</strong> Right-click the tray icon and select <strong>Start Server</strong>.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">Communication Port and Firewall Setup</h4>\n<p>In the AIBridge analytics plugin engine settings (<strong>Network Optix VMS Site Administration &gt; General &gt; Integrations &gt; Integrations Menu</strong>), set a unique port (9911). This port is the TCP port used for communication between the NX Witness AIBridge analytics plugin and AIBridge.</p>\n<p>If you're using the Windows firewall, add a new rule under <strong>Windows Firewall Setup &gt; Advanced Settings &gt; Inbound Rules &gt; New Rule</strong>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-weight:700;\">For Linux (Ubuntu x64 18.04, 20.04, 22.04)</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 4px;\">Download the AIBridge analytics Linux plugin from the customer portal, then run the following commands in order:</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<pre style=\"background:#0e1420;color:#d7dee8;padding:14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.7;\">tar zxvf aibridge_plugin_v1.1.0_20230808.tar.gz\ncd aibridge_plugin_v1.1.0_20230808\nchmod 755 install.sh\nsudo ./install.sh</pre>\n</div>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Running <code>install.sh</code> automatically detects the Ubuntu OS version along with NX Witness and NX MetaVMS, and installs the required packages automatically. Once the module finishes installing following the script's instructions, restart the VMS to complete plugin installation.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.3 Adding an NX API Account</h3>\n<p>Add an NX <strong>api</strong> account for AIBridge to use. AIBridge's default authentication method is Digest.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. NX is planning to end support for Digest authentication soon and will only offer Bearer authentication going forward.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.4 Enabling the AIBridge Analytics Plugin on a Video Channel</h3>\n<p>In the NX client's left panel, right-click the camera you want AIBridge to process and select <strong>Camera Settings</strong>.</p>\n<p>On the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab, enable the aibridge analytics plugin.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:230px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Enable Metadata</span><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    <span>Ignore Metadata (unanalyzed face objects)</span><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    <span>Ignore Metadata (unanalyzed plate objects)</span><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    <span>Show Counter</span><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    <span>Enable Debug Dump</span><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    <span>Metadata Timestamp correction</span><input value=\"0\" disabled style=\"width:70px;\">\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>AIBridge analytics plugin &ndash; Integrations tab settings</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Enable Metadata</strong> &ndash; recommended for installation or debugging purposes only. Even when this option is disabled, objects for which an event occurred are still displayed (saved) automatically.</li>\n<li><strong>Ignore Metadata (unanalyzed face objects)</strong> &ndash; ignores unanalyzed face information.</li>\n<li><strong>Ignore Metadata (unanalyzed plate objects)</strong> &ndash; ignores unanalyzed license plate (LPR) information.</li>\n<li><strong>Show Counter</strong> &ndash; displays the number of times the event has occurred.</li>\n<li><strong>Enable Debug Dump</strong> &ndash; recommended for installation or debugging purposes only. Large log files may accumulate under <code>{NxInstallPath}\\</code>, typically <code>C:\\Program Files\\Network Optix\\Nx Witness\\MediaServer\\</code>. Should be disabled in production environments.</li>\n<li><strong>Metadata Timestamp correction</strong> &ndash; metadata (bounding boxes) is buffered for the configured duration. (Metadata display is delayed by the configured time.) To resolve delay issues, see section 5.1.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.5 Enabling Video Channel Recording</h3>\n<p>An analytics channel that isn't set to record can't make use of the EVENT and OBJECT panels in NX VMS.</p>\n\n<h2>3. AIBridge Configuration</h2>\n<p>This section configures the Loitering Person app for integration with the AIBridge NX VMS plugin.</p>\n<p>AIBridge provides over 50 AI applications for various use cases &ndash; see the full app list at the <a href=\"https://indoai.com/goods/catalog?page=1&searchMode=catalog&category=c0006&per=40&sorting=ranking&filter_display=lattice&code=0006\">catalog link</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.1 Video Source Setup</h3>\n<p>Configure (add) a video stream. You can add a video stream using ONVIF device discovery, or by directly adding the IP camera's RTSP stream address.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.2 Configuring the Loitering Person App</h3>\n<p>Click <strong>Add Rule</strong> to add an event video source, then configure the event settings.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">AIBridge's <strong>Event Name</strong> field is displayed as the <strong>Caption</strong> field in NX VMS. It's recommended to enter a name that clearly identifies the event. Objects are tagged as shown in the figure. You can also configure detailed rules by comparing text against the Caption field when registering a rule.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.3 Adding the NX Plugin Action Handler</h3>\n<p>Add an action setting and select <strong>VMS / Nx Plugin</strong> as the action type.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>VMS / Nx Plugin</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>Edit the VMS IP and account information:</strong> enter the previously registered <strong>api</strong> account information (case sensitive) and use the login button to test it. On a successful test, a green connected status indicator appears.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">Nx Plugin</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Host</span><input value=\"192.168.101.20\" disabled>\n      <span>Username</span><input value=\"api\" disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input disabled>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"margin-top:8px;color:var(--green);font-size:12px;\">&#9679; Connected</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Login</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>VMS IP and account settings &ndash; test the connection with the Login button</figcaption>\n</div>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. AIBridge's default authentication method is Digest. If NX ends support for Digest authentication, Bearer authentication must be used instead.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Additional object information can be delivered to NX VMS through the message example field (e.g. license plate recognition information from the LPR app, group information).</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">Channel Mapping</h4>\n<p>You need to link channel information between AIBridge and NX VMS. Once the channel ID is entered correctly, clicking the <strong>Cameras Update</strong> button shows a green connected status.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>AIBridge Channel</th><th>NX Channel ID (Camera ID)</th><th>Status</th></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 1</td><td><input value=\"{6f2a19c0-...}\" disabled style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:11px;width:100%;\"></td><td style=\"color:var(--green);\">&#9679; Connected</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 2</td><td><input disabled style=\"width:100%;\"></td><td style=\"color:var(--text-muted);\">Disconnected</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<figcaption>The NX Channel ID (Camera ID) can be copied from the camera settings menu in NX VMS</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>Once every setting is complete, click the save button at the bottom of the web page.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If you don't click the save button, the settings are not saved.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>4. Demo</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.1 Live</h3>\n<p>Objects for which a Loitering Person event occurred are displayed in the NX VMS OBJECTS panel.</p>\n<p>Saved objects can be searched using the <strong>Advanced</strong> menu under Object in NX VMS. If an object doesn't appear, enable <strong>Show on Items</strong> from the popup menu in the video window.</p>\n<p>You can then manually specify the ROI area. This will automatically sync with AIBridge's ROI (zone) information through a future AIBridge FW upgrade.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.2 Adding an NX VMS Event Rule</h3>\n<p>Add Camera Rules in NX VMS and configure a desktop notification action, and you can check the event in the NX VMS EVENTS panel.</p>\n<p>Pay attention to the <strong>Event Type</strong> setting when registering a camera rule &ndash; if the app configured in AIBridge and the Event Type don't match, the event won't fire.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If the AIBridge Analytics plugin isn't up to date, the App Event Type supported by the AIBridge FW may not be available. In that case, select <strong>Event</strong> as the Event Type.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>5. FAQ</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">5.1 Resolving Video Delay</h3>\n<p>This section explains how to adjust the timestamp in Network Optix when the bounding box doesn't line up with the object (i.e. when a delay occurs).</p>\n<p>Right-click the camera and select <strong>Camera Settings</strong>. Set <strong>Metadata Timestamp</strong> to an appropriate value and click <strong>OK</strong>. A value between 500 and 1000 is generally recommended, though this can vary depending on your network environment.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">5.2 Controlling AIBridge's ARM/DISARM State Using a Soft Trigger</h3>\n<p>You can control AIBridge's ARM / DISARM state from Nx Witness using the Soft Trigger feature provided by Nx Witness. A few settings are required to use this feature &ndash; follow the steps below.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Select the AIBridge channel you want to control, right-click it, and select <strong>Camera Rules&hellip;</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>Add</strong> button at the top right and configure a Soft Trigger. Before configuring it, refer to the device's built-in Device Control API for details &ndash; be careful when setting the method and URL, since incorrect syntax may prevent the feature from working correctly.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Tip. Besides ARM / DISARM, you can use AIBridge's Generic Event and Virtual Alarm as action handlers for a variety of purposes &ndash; turning warning lights on or off, playing warning broadcasts, and more. Refer to the System API document under AI Bridge's Document section.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Once configured, a button appears in the bottom right of the live screen &ndash; click it to use the Soft Trigger you configured.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Note. Due to AIBridge's internal authentication structure, if you're using a derived (white-labeled) Nx VMS, you'll need to add that derived name on a hidden page in AIBridge. This doesn't apply to a non-derived Nx VMS.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">In Nx VMS, check the Client name under System Administration, then add that phrase on AIBridge's hidden page. Matching is case-sensitive, and entering just part of the phrase is enough. Hidden page: <code>https://&lt;AIBridgeIP:WebPort&gt;/#/pages/digest</code></p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>6. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>v1.03 &ndash; Changed the default plugin service port: 9011 &rarr; 9911.</li>\n<li>v1.04 &ndash; Changed the minimum supported NX Witness VMS version (4.2.0.32840).</li>\n<li>v1.05 &ndash; Added NX 5.1 support, added Ubuntu x64 18.04, 20.04, 22.04 support.</li>\n<li>v1.06 &ndash; Added section 4, FAQ.</li>\n<li>v1.07 &ndash; Added section 5.2, FAQ.</li>\n<li>v1.08 &ndash; Changed API authentication method: Digest &rarr; Bearer Token.</li>\n<li>v1.09 &ndash; Updated API authentication details.</li>\n</ul>";
